.TH tunl n 0.2 tclutils
.SH tclutils::tunl
.PP
\fBnl\fR\-like line numbering in pure Tcl.
.SS API
.CS
::tclutils::tunl::text text ?options?
::tclutils::tunl::file path ?options?
.CE
.PP
Options: \fB\-style all|nonempty|none\fR (default \fBnonempty\fR), \fB\-start N\fR (default 1), \fB\-increment N\fR (default 1), \fB\-width N\fR (default 6), \fB\-separator S\fR (default tab). A trailing newline is preserved and is not numbered.
.PP
\fB\-start\fR and \fB\-increment\fR are integers (negative allowed, any size); \fB\-width\fR is an integer of at least 1. The number is right\-aligned in \fB\-width\fR columns.
.SS Errors
.TS
l l.
Case	\fB\-errorcode\fR
\fB\-style\fR not \fBall\fR, \fBnonempty\fR, \fBnone\fR	\fB{TCLUTILS TUNL STYLE}\fR
\fB\-start\fR not an integer	\fB{TCLUTILS TUNL START}\fR
\fB\-increment\fR not an integer	\fB{TCLUTILS TUNL INCREMENT}\fR
\fB\-width\fR not an integer >= 1	\fB{TCLUTILS TUNL WIDTH}\fR
unknown option	\fB{TCLUTILS COMMON OPTION \-name}\fR
.TE
.SS CLI
.CS
tclsh bin/tunl.tcl -width 3 -separator " " file.txt
.CE
